{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner N1 revision 3, 2026-10-04. Complete read of all 912 lines/50,359 bytes at 31eef8f3022d56a45073c5aba2b9b7c28d63ccba; only this note changed from b4b06d26, with frozen 006 files and separate provenance unchanged, and that delta passes whitespace checking. The actual recorded empty/all-merge-bases comparison, qualified legacy candidate, independent head-file access, separate set/work bounds, normal encoded-byte limits, bounded blob acquisition and Room-evidence wording now materially apply a1db261a. Preserve them. This remains planning source, without adoption or implementation authorization.\n\nOne remaining data dependency matters to the promised public change-history adapter. At d691, changes.ts patch() (275–306) discovers each commit's own paths by treeDiff(parent,self) before reading file contents. Its interdiff (197 onward) compares both complete patch path sets. The proposed commits response supplies no changed paths, and file can fetch only a known path. The proposal's net changed paths and changedSince between heads cannot discover a path changed by one commit and restored by another. Thus section 5.4's small adapter cannot yet construct the advertised commit snapshots completely. Extend the proposed input contract with a bounded per-commit changed-path read (or an explicitly equivalent bounded metadata result), scoped to this recorded generation and a validated commit in its history. It should identify the exact commit and first-parent/empty-root comparison, expose statuses and rename source paths needed for both snapshots, and have query-bound item/encoded-byte pagination and explicit too-large/unavailable results. No arbitrary tree or blob-ID API is needed. Update the exact types/methods/routes/rules, transport parity, A1–A7 dependencies and client completeness wording together. Include a compact transient-path witness within the existing history acceptance, rather than a new test suite or row sweep. If a bounded complete path set cannot be obtained, the client reports the patch/interdiff incomplete and never calls it unchanged.\n\nFinish three small consistency repairs while doing that: (a) Section 4 still says several bases can never reproduce changed with one commit; replace this inherited sentence with the fact that the union need not equal any single base, but can. (b) Section 7's claim that a single returned path always fits is justified only by an output-path bound, not the 4,096-byte bound on a caller's input. Source ids.ts defines RepoPath syntax but no byte bound, and treediff concatenates repository entry names. Specify a normal read-size result for a returned path that is too long or cannot fit alone, without truncating its identity, dropping it silently or changing old proposal admission. A page either advances within its bound or returns that explicit size result. (c) Align the whole-tree disclosure in section 6.1 with every permitted snapshot in 5.2, including head and recorded bases when the history set is empty. Resolve the R-ART-1 legacy set description against the explicit table of 5.1 rather than accidentally admitting all ancestors as a different set.\n\nNo further broad research or runtime probe is requested. Keep the original full matrix, no-transcript independent review, line-bound question, revision/evidence/publication story, all MCP scope and private C1 boundary. Exact independent design review and adoption still precede implementing commissions. Current all-47 release review at d691, the reviewer restriction, highest test-overhead priority and first useful Jam readiness are unaffected. No tests, build, installation, provider action, source edit or root commit was performed.","body":{"head":"31eef8f3022d56a45073c5aba2b9b7c28d63ccba","no_git_artifact":"true","scope":"N1 revision 3 complete read; bounded per-commit path discovery and remaining contract alignment.","source_approval":"none"}}